{"title":"2006 Romanian NMO Problems/Grade 7/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Romanian_NMO_Problems/Grade_7/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a set of positive integers with at least 2 elements. It is given that for any numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/29485b6f96ad867ccef806c88f5e0ef2fa031fda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/6550f4db3bccfcf0062b37b540bb0c9ecae03777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ [a,b] }{ a- b } \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"81\" height=\"42\" />, where by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> we have denoted the least common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has <i>exactly</i> two elements.\n</p><p><i>Marius Gherghu, Slatina</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Romanian_NMO_Problems/Grade_7/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is finite; for the sake of contradiction, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is infinite. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/66705dd209e625e2717f8580bfe38cc2010e56fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e238e0fdc44e9c91a2a99e0026f8a67a1443cc9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a167ae28983caf6ebba09fab02d97c64ce79a43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e27305fe4a3d547805eb64db15baac6616deb28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = GCD(n,a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f7434aa5a91b66cf62c51f017fa9895bba89f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[n,a]}{n-a} = \\frac{na}{g(n-a)} = \\frac{a}{g} + \\frac{a^{2}}{g(n-a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"269\" height=\"43\" /> is an integer for arbitrarily large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />; but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183b759d4be21dd576756512ad3be493cb3e4930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^{2}}{g(n-a)} &lt; \\frac{a^{2}}{n-a} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"173\" height=\"43\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a17036a4a0d18b878d17e4a59953bcdd585365a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; a^{2}+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is finite.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e31a6d551914e2a240995edf06a23743622cfa7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7da572d60053bdb3ab92f2dda44f87cd9dc78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />; let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca6db3efd0d5b264e05aed03620dff28d85c4ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = GCD(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d24fb768fb5e39eedb6e5e5cf51c8dc6d5bfca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} = x/g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fdaf1165b54b0605550f9cc83a562817d5a59810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{0} = y/g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92d61210d46d883cbf08eb733186a7046b3bddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[x,y]}{x-y} = \\frac{xy}{g(x-y)} = \\frac{x_{0}y_{0}}{x_{0}-y_{0}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"227\" height=\"45\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b095fc9e89a57e2ed480d857efe13b477b0f2cc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} - y_{0} &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a7a9364352da773c714d32ba7e617d35c88b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} - y_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"11\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e669253c4e7faee3f83a492830f13b68c47b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9bed9ab9e3bc69f63f6469dce000f0d83c3fa38a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides neither because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e669253c4e7faee3f83a492830f13b68c47b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9bed9ab9e3bc69f63f6469dce000f0d83c3fa38a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> are relatively prime. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/5808ca39b800cab18d55d28c52480c5e6e1373fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{0} - y_{0} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4a8996555d2f3137a96d412848b99be48a6ff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aadb384615033596d45ce4a0ad13ba549b84ffc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xy}{(x-y)^{2}} \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"105\" height=\"39\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e31a6d551914e2a240995edf06a23743622cfa7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7da572d60053bdb3ab92f2dda44f87cd9dc78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest element and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the largest element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef78f2a4f22b19a8d95d409103df76380f5e058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ab}{(a-b)^{2}} \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"101\" height=\"42\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f24aa737529c3e0d0cea4e43b3cbe290dd9418d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\le \\frac{ab}{(a-b)^{2}} \\le a \\implies b \\le (a-b)^{2} \\le a \\implies 0 \\le (a-b)^{2}-b \\le a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"546\" height=\"42\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a697bfdeadf2105048670e6f6c7d4dc6878dc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> so either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734469ee569cc1776295ae2bde69667b0f9354ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = (a-b)^{2}-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb72aa8107c9945a32162054c6e396f54f9708aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^{2}-b = a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895590b71eb0d7ffaa5ed8b32e6527141bacbcad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e238e0fdc44e9c91a2a99e0026f8a67a1443cc9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c043bb591847dd1e5b961b81ece87d299212b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; n &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/2676c64c815d86a4c222934a4629598bacfcd210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^{2} = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/1/0716ddd1693702490108b178d9c899406721308d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[n,a]}{a-n} = \\frac{an}{(a-n)^{2}} &gt; \\frac{ab}{(a-b)^{2}} = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"262\" height=\"43\" />, contradiction. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356aadc86c58266ba3bffcb7373513ea608b77f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^{2} = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" />, we can without loss of generality assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the second largest element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c4284eb8b0669a125050de78869168457b52d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[n,a]}{a-n} = \\frac{an}{(a-n)^{2}} &gt; \\frac{an}{(a-b)^{2}} = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"263\" height=\"43\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec10997a9afbe0de21642168e73526ecbce35f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{an}{(a-n)^{2}} = a \\implies n = (a-n)^{2} \\implies (a-b)^{2} = a = (a-n)^{2} + (a-n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"562\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d975a2935a43e6f24f21faa758e2d57c0a94c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^{2} - (a-n)^{2} = a-n \\implies (n-b)(a-b+a-n) = a-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"504\" height=\"19\" /> which is a contradiction since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c97a189bd0c877ba2f98e0938ed8e7d2aac496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b,n-b &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Romanian_NMO_Problems/Grade_7/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Romanian_NMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 Romanian NMO Problems\">2006 Romanian NMO Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018052617\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 333/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12073/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3592:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018052617 and revision id 40298. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}